                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68d7e374-3416-32e7-8a57-f5a9f9da1c87",
                        "entry_id": "186ad3ef-3e72-36d4-800c-60ebc3a02047",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lacking passion; dispassionate"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "922b39c3-f0a1-432e-8c65-2af10d5c34f7",
                                "sense_id": "68d7e374-3416-32e7-8a57-f5a9f9da1c87",
                                "text": "Various old ladies in the neighbourhood spoke of him as The Last of the Patriarchs. So grey, so slow, so quiet, so impassionate, so very bumpy in the head, Patriarch was the word for him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aeb4301d-a765-4c68-81d2-4946817a3281",
                                "sense_id": "68d7e374-3416-32e7-8a57-f5a9f9da1c87",
                                "text": "“Try to serve well and to show yourself worthy,” he added, turning sternly to Borís. “I am glad— Are you here on leave?” he recited, in his impassionate voice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5eb1416e-1575-41ce-beda-9dfa93478a6d",
                                "sense_id": "68d7e374-3416-32e7-8a57-f5a9f9da1c87",
                                "text": "From a scholarly standpoint, the book was poorly written: Scholarly works demand keen attention to logical consistency while maintaining an impersonal, impassionate voice; and while the Course certainly lack humour, it is anything but impassionate, and far from being logically consistent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
